### 4.4 list_conversations

When `transport.history.enabled` is true, a client may request authenticated conversation summaries; when disabled or unsupported by the store, the server answers `UNSUPPORTED` rather than an empty list. The request is answered independently of the per-session turn lock, so a history response does not wait for a streaming turn ([validated by: refuses conversation listing when history is enabled but the store cannot list](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L112), [validated by: answers a conversation list while a user turn is still streaming](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L74)). The server takes the user id from the authenticated connection and never from the frame.

| Field    | Type   | Required | Description                                 |
| -------- | ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| `type`   | string | Yes      | `"list_conversations"`                      |
| `limit`  | number | No       | Integer from 1 through 200                  |
| `before` | object | No       | Cursor with ISO `updatedAt` and `sessionId` |

## 5. Server-to-Client Messages

### 5.1 connected

Sent exactly once after a successful handshake. See Section 2.3.

| Field            | Type     | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |
| ---------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `type`           | string   | `"connected"`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |
| `sessionId`      | string   | UUID v4 identifying the session                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |
| `message`        | string   | Human-readable greeting                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |
| `examplePrompts` | string[] | Example queries derived from registered tool definitions                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |
| `resumed`        | boolean  | Present only with resume enabled: whether the requested conversation was rejoined                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |
| `entryCount`     | number   | Present only when `resumed` is `true`: how many stored entries the replay covers, skipped ones included                                                                                                                                                                                             |
| `resumeFailure`  | string   | Present only when the connection named an id and `resumed` is `false`: `expired` when the caller's own session aged out, `unknown` otherwise. `unknown` deliberately covers both an id the server never issued and one that is not the caller's, so the answer reveals nothing about ids that exist |

### 5.2 conversation_list

Carries one authenticated user's conversation metadata and no conversation content. It is sent only in response to `list_conversations`; the server never accepts a user id from that frame. A deployer enables this disclosure explicitly with `transport.history.enabled` ([validated by: answers a conversation list while a user turn is still streaming](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L74)).

| Field           | Type                  | Description                                    |
| --------------- | --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| `type`          | string                | `"conversation_list"`                          |
| `conversations` | ConversationSummary[] | Summaries with ISO `createdAt` and `updatedAt` |

### 5.3 entry_upsert

